<title>UK: INTERVIEW-SW Water at ease on leakage goals.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW-SW Water at ease on leakage goals.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South West Water Plc said on Thursday it was not unduly concerned about the British government's plan to set mandatory targets for cutting leakage at water companies.</p>
<p>&quot;As far as we know, there is nothing in those proposals which will give us cause for major concern,&quot; finance director Ken Hill said in an interview.</p>
<p>He added that the company was waiting for the government to detail the plan, which was aimed at easing Britain's current drought.</p>
</text>
